# --- Encrypted token vault (Phase G) ---
# Set LLM_VAULT_PASSPHRASE to enable durable, restart-safe token storage.
# Tokens (LLM provider keys + per-agency model overrides) are written to an
# encrypted file on the server. One GPG/AES key covers the whole server; the
# *file layout* is per-user (users[userId].llm[role]) so future multi-user
# auth drops in without reshaping the data.
#
# Cipher selection (automatic, at boot):
#   - gpg installed + LLM_VAULT_PASSPHRASE set  -> GPG symmetric (--symmetric)
#   - else, LLM_VAULT_PASSPHRASE set            -> AES-256-GCM (Node built-in)
#   - else                                       -> vault disabled (in-memory only)
LLM_VAULT_PASSPHRASE=
# Optional: override the default path (.vault/llm-tokens.gpg) and user key.
# LLM_VAULT_PATH=/abs/path/to/llm-tokens.gpg
# LLM_VAULT_USER=default
